[0mThe provided material describes several additional experiments, but it doesn't include a dedicated ablation study of MetaGPT's components. The closest results are below.

**Executability comparison (scored 1–4)**
- MetaGPT averaged 3.9, well ahead of ChatDev (2.1) and AutoGPT, LangChain and AgentVerse (1.0 each).
- MetaGPT scored 4 on every task except Flappy bird, where it scored 3. These tasks were the Tank battle, 2048, Snake and Brick breaker games, Excel data processing and CRUD management.
- ChatDev scored 4 only on Excel data processing.

**Different LLM backends on SoftwareDev**

| Backend | Open source | Time (s) | # Lines | Executability | Revisions |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| GPT-3.5 | No | 75.18 | 161.6 | 2.8 | 2.4 |
| GPT-4 | No | 552.94 | 178.2 | 3.8 | 1.2 |
| Deepseek Coder 33B | Yes | 1186.20 | 120.2 | 1.4 | 2.6 |

- GPT-4 gave the best executability (3.8) and needed the fewest revisions (1.2).
- GPT-3.5 was the fastest, but its executability was lower (2.8).
- The open-source Deepseek Coder 33B was the slowest and had the lowest executability (1.4).

**Instruction level (high-level vs. detailed prompts, 5 SoftwareDev tasks)**

| Prompt | # Words | Time (s) | Token usage | # Lines | Executability | Productivity | Revisions |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| High-level | 13.2 | 552.9 | 28,384.2 | 178.2 | 3.8 | 163.8 | 1.2 |
| Detailed | 42.2 | 567.8 | 29,657.0 | 257.0 | 4.0 | 118.0 | 1.6 |

- Productivity is token usage divided by total code lines, so lower is better.
- Detailed prompts produced better software, with executability of 4.0 and a lower productivity ratio, because the requirements and functions were clearer.
- Simple high-level inputs still produced good software, with executability of 3.8, which is comparable to the detailed-prompt case.

**GPT variants on HumanEval**
- The baseline is GPT-4's reported 67% HumanEval score.
- GPT-4 (gpt-4-0613) and GPT-3.5-Turbo (gpt-3.5-turbo-0613) were each tested five times under several conditions:
  - (A) calling the API directly with the HumanEval prompt;
  - (B) calling the API and parsing the code from the response with regex;
  - (C) adding a system prompt that tells the model to respond only with Python code.
- The text is cut off before any results for these conditions.
